    "result_text": "Build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a per-city capacity rule that rejects owner creation with **409 Conflict** when the target city already contains 50+ owners, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files (small, cohesive units \u2014 no existing function modified):**\n- `RejectOwnerCityAtCapacity.java` \u2014 a single-method step that counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, trimmed) and throws when 50 are found. Since the new owner isn't saved yet, a city with exactly 50 rejects the 51st.\n- `CityAtCapacityException.java` \u2014 checked exception (extends `Exception`) carrying the 409 semantics.\n- `CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 mirrors the existing duplicate-handler pattern, responding 409 with a `ProblemDetail`.\n- `...CityAtCapacityException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**One edit to existing config:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `rejectCityAtCapacity` step between the household-duplicate check and customer-code assignment (governed by the same transaction).\n\n**Structural impact:** No existing function was grown or touched \u2014 behaviour is added as new classes each with cyclomatic complexity ~1 and near-zero surrounding context (WMC_other). The only edit to an existing file is a declarative YAML step insertion. Full test suite passes.",
